{"formatVersion":{"major":1,"minor":1,"patch":0},"patch":{"connections":[{"from":[6,"output"],"to":[7,"input0"]},{"from":[7,"output0"],"to":[9,"radius"]},{"from":[8,"output"],"to":[10,"input"]},{"from":[9,"output"],"to":[11,"input"]},{"from":[10,"output"],"to":[13,"shape"]},{"from":[13,"output0"],"to":[12,"input2"]},{"from":[11,"output"],"to":[14,"shape"]},{"from":[14,"output0"],"to":[12,"input1"]},{"from":[12,"output"],"to":[15,"input"]},{"from":[6,"output"],"to":[8,"radius"]}],"meta":{"author":"","category":null,"description":"This patch explains what this node does.","displayName":"Modulo","identifier":"a58095d8-ea67-45e7-888f-9e177034b0ed","licenseFile":"","licenseName":"","mail":"","quality":32856,"resolution":{"height":1080,"width":1920},"thumbnail":"","url":"","vendor":""},"nextNodeId":16,"nodes":{"1":{"attributes":{"font-size":{"type":"number","value":19},"text":{"type":"text","value":"MODULO\nWith the modulo operation you can divide a number and output the remainder.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n•  The Saw oscillator is set to unipolar in the inspector. This provides us with values running from 0 to 1 before jumping back to 0.\n• The output of the oscillator modulates the radius of the yellow ring.\n•The output is also sent to the Modulo node, where it gets divided by 0.5 and the remainder is sent out.\n• This results in the red ring expanding half way through the motion of the yellow ring as well as growing only half the size of the red ring.\n"}},"bounds":{"height":248.7570648193359375,"width":875.70135498046875,"x":111.482757568359375,"y":137.1116943359375},"class":{"id":"77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374","version":0},"clock":"video","constants":{},"hidden":[],"name":"Comment"},"10":{"attributes":{"instances":{"type":"number","value":1},"mode":{"type":"choice","value":"Inner"}},"bounds":{"height":58,"width":195,"x":774.033447265625,"y":409.99462890625},"class":{"id":"77697265-ab950887-37ee-4fd2-9487-c856b6b75c83","version":0},"clock":"video","constants"